Software this depends on
------------------------

  * **Givaro**: exact arithmetic over finite fields and over the rationals,
    developed by the CASYS team at the Laboratoire Jean Kuntzmann, Université
    Grenoble Alpes. https://casys.gricad-pages.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/givaro/
    Used, not vendored: it is installed from the system package manager and no
    part of it is copied into this repository.

  * **GMP**, on which Givaro's integer and rational arithmetic rests.

FFLAS-FFPACK, from the same team, was used for rank in an earlier revision and
removed once a reduction against an echelon-form basis measured faster at these
sizes. It is no longer a dependency.

The solvers this can call, and does not ship, are named where they are used:
kissat, CryptoMiniSat, CaDiCaL and cvc5 for the satisfiability strand, drat-trim
for checking its refutations, and CBC, GLPK, lp_solve or Gurobi for the integer
programme layer. Each is located on PATH at run time, and a run says which one
answered.


Timings
-------

Every time reported in this repository was measured on a single core of a 12th
Gen Intel Core i5-12450H at 2.2 GHz. The protocol, the flags a published number
depends on, and the roughly thirteen per cent this chassis varies from thermal
throttling alone, are in **MEASURING.md**. Counts are asserted by the test suite
and reproduce anywhere; timings are not, and are not claimed to.

PLinOpt's operators
-------------------
fixtures/plinopt/ is thirteen `.sms` matrices copied unmodified from the `data/`
directory of **PLinOpt**, by Jean-Guillaume Dumas, Bruno Grenet, Clément Pernet
and Alexandre Sedoglavic, https://github.com/jgdumas/plinopt. **CeCILL-B**, whose
Article 5.3.1 asks that a copy of the agreement and the warranty and liability
disclaimers of Articles 8 and 9 travel with the files; the licence text is in
that directory, as PermLib's is in its own.

They are the interoperability, not decoration: the exchange with the reference
toolchain is exercised by the test suite against his bytes rather than against
something written here to resemble them. What each file carries is
fixtures/plinopt/README.md.

PermLib
-------
vendor/permlib/ is Thomas Rehn's PermLib, the include/ tree of upstream commit
2b4e468e24a059e3659bc095293df0cd363a22f5, unmodified. BSD 3-clause; the licence
and the author list travel with it in vendor/permlib/.

It is here for one function, permlib_api.h's smallestSetImage, which is
S. A. Linton, "Finding the smallest image of a set", ISSAC 2004, credited in
PermLib's own include/permlib/search/orbit_lex_min_search.h. The reduction that
uses it is methods/bilinear_rank/oracle_guided_search/subspace_canon.h.
